{
  "id": "21277_hougou",
  "headword": "{縫合|ほうごう}",
  "reading": "ほうごう",
  "romaji": "hougou",
  "part_of_speech": "noun, suru verb",
  "gloss": "suturing; stitching",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "suturing; stitching; sewing up (a wound)",
      "explanation": "The medical procedure of closing a wound or surgical incision by sewing it together with thread or other materials."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "21277_hougou_ex1",
      "japanese": "{傷口|きずぐち}を{縫合|ほうごう}した。",
      "english": "The wound was sutured.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21277_hougou_ex2",
      "japanese": "{手術|しゅじゅつ}の{最後|さいご}に{切開部|せっかいぶ}を{縫合|ほうごう}する。",
      "english": "At the end of the surgery, the incision is sutured closed.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "21277_hougou_ex3",
      "japanese": "{縫合|ほうごう}した{部分|ぶぶん}の{糸|いと}は{一週間後|いっしゅうかんご}に{抜|ぬ}く{予定|よてい}だ。",
      "english": "The stitches in the sutured area are scheduled to be removed in one week.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A compound of {縫|ほう} (to sew) and {合|ごう} (to join together). A medical term used in hospitals and clinics. While it is a technical word, it is commonly understood by the general public since stitching wounds is a familiar medical procedure.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {縫合|ほうごう}する: to suture\n- {縫合|ほうごう}{糸|し}: suture thread\n- {傷口|きずぐち}を{縫合|ほうごう}する: to stitch a wound\n- {縫合|ほうごう}を{解|と}く: to remove stitches\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {抜糸|ばっし}: removal of stitches — the follow-up procedure after {縫合|ほうごう}\n- {切開|せっかい}: incision — cutting open tissue, the opposite action\n- {傷口|きずぐち}: wound, cut — what gets sutured",
